# LAMMPS input script for bicrystal Fe phase transformation simulation
# Material: iron (Fe), bcc, lattice constant 2.866 Å

# --------------------- Initialization ---------------------
units metal
atom_style atomic
boundary p p p

# --------------------- Simulation cell ---------------------
region box block 0 100 0 20 0 20 units box
create_box 1 box
Created orthogonal box = (0 0 0) to (100 20 20)
  1 by 1 by 1 MPI processor grid

# --------------------- Left grain (x = 0 to 50) with [100] orientation ---------------------
region left block 0 50 0 20 0 20 units box
lattice bcc 2.866
Lattice spacing in x,y,z = 2.866 2.866 2.866
create_atoms 1 region left
Created 1715 atoms
  using lattice units in orthogonal box = (0 0 0) to (100 20 20)
  create_atoms CPU = 0.000 seconds

# --------------------- Right grain (x = 50 to 100) rotated 15° about z-axis ---------------------
# Use custom lattice with rotated basis vectors
# cos(15°) = 0.9659258, sin(15°) = 0.2588190
lattice custom 2.866   a1 0.9659258 0.2588190 0.0   a2 -0.2588190 0.9659258 0.0   a3 0.0 0.0 1.0   basis 0.0 0.0 0.0   basis 0.5 0.5 0.5
Lattice spacing in x,y,z = 3.5101186 3.5101186 2.866
region right block 50 100 0 20 0 20 units box
create_atoms 1 region right
